          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The low FODMAP diet is primarily used to manage symptoms of Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) including bloating, gas, abdominal pain, diarrhea, and constipation. It should be followed under the guidance of a registered dietitian." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
